                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Using the Pythagorean identity, complete the statement: ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "1+\\tan^2 x=",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "$\\sec^2 x$",
                  "width": 13
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ",",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sec^2 x$",
          "worked": "$$1+\\tan^2 x=\\sec^2 x$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence find $\\int\\tan^2 x\\,dx$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan x-x+C$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\int\\tan^2 x\\,dx&=\\int(\\sec^2 x-1)\\,dx\\\\&=\\tan x-x+C\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Simplify $1-\\sin^2 x$, and hence find the value of $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\frac{2}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,dx$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1-\\sin^2 x=\\cos^2 x$; integral value $2\\sqrt3$.",
          "worked": "$$1-\\sin^2 x=\\cos^2 x$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{1-\\sin^2 x}&=\\frac{2}{\\cos^2 x}\\\\&=2\\sec^2 x\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\frac{2}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,dx&=\\int_0^{\\pi/3}2\\sec^2 x\\,dx\\\\&=[2\\tan x]_0^{\\pi/3}\\\\&=2\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{3}-2\\tan0\\\\&=2\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
